---
// Final Quiz component - A fun, interactive 12-question knowledge test
---

<div class="final-quiz" id="final-quiz">
  <div class="quiz-intro" id="quiz-intro">
    <div class="intro-emoji">🎓</div>
    <h2>Merge Queue Mastery Exam</h2>
    <p>12 questions. No pressure. Okay, maybe a little pressure.</p>
    <p class="intro-sub">Test your knowledge and earn your diploma!</p>

    <div class="name-input-section">
      <label for="candidate-name">Enter your name for the diploma:</label>
      <input
        type="text"
        id="candidate-name"
        placeholder="Your Name"
        maxlength="40"
        autocomplete="name"
      />
      <span class="name-privacy">Not stored anywhere — just for your diploma!</span>
    </div>

    <button class="start-btn" id="start-quiz" type="button">
      🚀 Begin the Challenge
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz-main" id="quiz-main" style="display: none">
    <div class="quiz-header">
      <div class="progress-container">
        <div class="progress-bar">
          <div class="progress-fill" id="progress-fill"></div>
        </div>
        <span class="progress-text" id="progress-text">Question 1 / 12</span>
      </div>
      <div class="score-display">
        <span class="score-label">Score:</span>
        <span class="score-value" id="current-score">0</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="questions-container" id="questions-container">
      <!-- Question 1: True/False -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="0">
        <div class="q-type">🎯 True or False</div>
        <h3>A merge queue tests your PR against <em>only</em> the tip of main, ignoring other queued PRs.</h3>
        <div class="options tf-options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            ✅ True
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            ❌ False
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>False!</strong> That's what regular CI does. A merge queue tests your PR against the <em>future</em> state of main—including all PRs ahead of you in the queue. That's the whole point! 🎯
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 2: Multiple Choice -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="1" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">🤔 Pick One</div>
        <h3>Two PRs pass CI individually, but break main when merged together. This is called:</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🐛 A regression bug
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            💥 A semantic conflict
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🔀 A merge conflict
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🤷 Bad luck
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Semantic conflict!</strong> Merge conflicts are caught by git. Semantic conflicts are silent killers—code changes that are syntactically valid but logically incompatible. 💥
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 3: Fill in the blank style -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="2" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">📝 Complete the Sentence</div>
        <h3>Speculative checks work by <span class="blank">______</span> that PRs ahead in the queue will pass.</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🔮 Predicting
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            🎲 Assuming
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🤞 Hoping
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            ⏳ Waiting until
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Assuming!</strong> Speculative checks assume PRs ahead will pass and start testing yours in parallel. If that assumption is wrong, your test is invalidated and re-run. Optimism with a safety net! 🎲
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 4: Scenario -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="3" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">🎬 Scenario Time</div>
        <h3>Your CI takes 30 minutes. With a basic queue (no batching, no speculative checks), what's the max throughput?</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🐌 16 PRs/day
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            🚶 48 PRs/day
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🏃 96 PRs/day
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🚀 Unlimited
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>48 PRs/day!</strong> 24 hours × 60 minutes ÷ 30 minutes = 48. Sequential processing means one PR at a time. Speculative checks or batching would increase this! 🚶
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 5: What happens -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="4" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">⚡ What Happens Next?</div>
        <h3>PR #2 fails in the queue. PR #3 was speculatively tested against [main + #1 + #2]. What happens to PR #3?</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            ✅ It merges (it passed!)
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            ❌ It's removed from queue
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            🔄 It's re-tested against [main + #1]
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            ⏸️ It waits for #2 to be fixed
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Re-tested!</strong> PR #3's test is now invalid—it was tested in a world where #2 existed. The queue automatically re-tests #3 with a new base that excludes #2. 🔄
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 6: True/False -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="5" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">🎯 True or False</div>
        <h3>Batching saves CI costs by testing multiple PRs with a single CI run.</h3>
        <div class="options tf-options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            ✅ True
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            ❌ False
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>True!</strong> If you batch 3 PRs together, you run CI once instead of thrice. That's 66% cost savings! The tradeoff: if the batch fails, you need to bisect to find the culprit. 💰
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 7: Emoji Match -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="6" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">🧩 Match the Feature</div>
        <h3>Which feature lets frontend and backend PRs merge independently without blocking each other?</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            📦 Batching
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🎲 Speculative checks
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            🛤️ Parallel queues
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🔢 Priority lanes
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Parallel queues!</strong> They let independent scopes (frontend, backend, docs) each have their own queue. Changes that don't affect each other don't wait for each other. 🛤️
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 8: Order -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="7" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">🏁 First Things First</div>
        <h3>What should you fix BEFORE adopting a merge queue?</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            🎲 Flaky tests
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            📝 PR templates
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🎨 Code style
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            📊 Test coverage (more is better)
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Flaky tests!</strong> A 2% flake rate means 1 in 50 queue runs fails randomly. With batching, flakes eject innocent PRs. Fix flakes first—aim for &lt;0.5% flake rate. 🎲
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 9: Company trivia -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="8" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">🏢 Industry Knowledge</div>
        <h3>Which company's merge queue (SubmitQueue) uses machine learning to predict change success?</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🛒 Shopify
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            🚗 Uber
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🐙 GitHub
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🔍 Google
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Uber!</strong> Their SubmitQueue uses ML to predict which changes are likely to pass, optimizing build scheduling. They went from 52% green to 99% green on their iOS mainline! 🚗
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 10: Monorepo -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="9" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">🏗️ Monorepo Mastery</div>
        <h3>In a monorepo, a PR touches both /frontend and /backend. With parallel queues, how should it be handled?</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🎲 Pick one queue randomly
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            🔗 Union: enter both queues simultaneously
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            ⛔ Reject cross-scope changes
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🌐 Use a global queue only
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Union strategy!</strong> The PR enters both queues and must pass in both before merging. This prevents a cross-scope change from breaking either scope while keeping queues mostly independent. 🔗
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 11: Two-step CI -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="10" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">🔄 Two-Step Thinking</div>
        <h3>In two-step CI, what's the purpose of the first step (PR CI)?</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            ⚡ Fast feedback: lint, unit tests, build
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🔒 Security scanning only
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            📊 Generate coverage reports
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🚀 Deploy to staging
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Fast feedback!</strong> Step 1 (PR CI) runs quick checks to give developers fast feedback. Step 2 (Queue CI) runs the full test suite against the real merge target. Speed + correctness! ⚡
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Question 12: Final boss -->
      <div class="question-card" data-q="11" style="display: none">
        <div class="q-type">👑 Final Boss Question</div>
        <h3>The "Not Rocket Science Rule" that inspired merge queues states:</h3>
        <div class="options">
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🧪 Test everything twice
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            🏃 Move fast and break things
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="true" type="button">
            ✅ Automatically maintain a repository that always passes all tests
          </button>
          <button class="option-btn" data-correct="false" type="button">
            📝 Document before you code
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="explanation" style="display: none">
          <strong>Correct!</strong> Graydon Hoare (Rust's creator) coined this in 2013 when building Bors. It's not rocket science to keep main green—just test before you merge. Simple in principle, powerful in practice! 👑
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="question-footer">
      <button class="next-btn" id="next-btn" type="button" disabled>
        Next Question →
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz-results" id="quiz-results" style="display: none">
    <div class="diploma-wrapper">
      <div class="diploma" id="diploma">
        <div class="diploma-bg"></div>
        <div class="diploma-ornament top-left">❧</div>
        <div class="diploma-ornament top-right">❧</div>
        <div class="diploma-ornament bottom-left">❧</div>
        <div class="diploma-ornament bottom-right">❧</div>
        <div class="diploma-content">
          <div class="diploma-left">
            <div class="diploma-icon">🎓</div>
            <div class="diploma-seal">
              <span class="seal-emoji">🏆</span>
              <span class="seal-text">CERTIFIED</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="diploma-center">
            <h2>Certificate of Achievement</h2>
            <div class="diploma-divider">
              <span class="divider-line"></span>
              <span class="divider-star">✦</span>
              <span class="divider-line"></span>
            </div>
            <p class="diploma-subtitle">This is to certify that</p>
            <div class="diploma-name" id="diploma-name">Distinguished Graduate</div>
            <p class="diploma-text">has demonstrated proficiency in</p>
            <p class="diploma-subject">Merge Queue Engineering</p>
          </div>

          <div class="diploma-right">
            <div class="score-badge">
              <span class="score-number" id="final-score">0</span>
              <span class="score-total">/12</span>
            </div>
            <div class="diploma-grade" id="diploma-grade">Merge Queue Master</div>
            <div class="diploma-meta">
              <div class="diploma-date" id="diploma-date"></div>
              <div class="diploma-source">merge-queue.academy</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="share-section">
      <p class="share-title">🎉 Share your achievement!</p>
      <div class="share-buttons">
        <button class="share-btn download" id="download-diploma" type="button">
          📥 Download Diploma
        </button>
        <button class="share-btn twitter" id="share-twitter" type="button">
          𝕏 Share on X
        </button>
        <button class="share-btn linkedin" id="share-linkedin" type="button">
          in Share on LinkedIn
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="share-toast" id="share-toast"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="results-breakdown" id="results-breakdown">
      <!-- Filled by JS -->
    </div>

    <div class="retry-section">
      <button class="retry-btn" id="retry-btn" type="button">
        🔄 Try Again
      </button>
      <a href="/" class="home-link">← Back to Academy</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .final-quiz {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 2rem auto;
  }

  /* Intro */
  .quiz-intro {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    background: var(--mqa-bg-subtle, #1a1d24);
    border: 1px solid var(--mqa-border-subtle, #272c37);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .intro-emoji {
    font-size: 4rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .quiz-intro h2 {
    font-family: var(--mqa-font-display, 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--mqa-text, #f0f2f5);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .quiz-intro h2::before,
  .diploma h2::before {
    display: none !important;
  }

  .quiz-intro p {
    color: var(--mqa-text-secondary, #b4bcd0);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .intro-sub {
    font-size: 0.95rem !important;
    color: var(--mqa-text-muted, #8891a5) !important;
    margin-top: 0.5rem !important;
  }

  .name-input-section {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .name-input-section label {
    color: var(--mqa-text-secondary, #b4bcd0);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .name-input-section input {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 300px;
    padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
    background: var(--mqa-bg-muted, #21252e);
    border: 2px solid var(--mqa-border, #323846);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--mqa-text, #f0f2f5);
    font-family: var(--mqa-font-display, 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    text-align: center;
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .name-input-section input:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
  }

  .name-input-section input::placeholder {
    color: var(--mqa-text-muted, #8891a5);
  }

  .name-privacy {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--mqa-text-muted, #8891a5);
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .start-btn {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 2.5rem;
    background: var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #0a0b0d;
    font-family: var(--mqa-font-display, 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .start-btn:hover {
    background: var(--mqa-accent-hover, #fbbf24);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  /* Main Quiz */
  .quiz-main {
    background: var(--mqa-bg-subtle, #1a1d24);
    border: 1px solid var(--mqa-border-subtle, #272c37);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .quiz-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .progress-container {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 200px;
  }

  .progress-bar {
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--mqa-bg-elevated, #282d38);
    border-radius: 3px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .progress-fill {
    height: 100%;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b), #fbbf24);
    width: 8.33%;
    transition: width 0.4s ease;
  }

  .progress-text {
    font-family: var(--mqa-font-mono, 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--mqa-text-muted, #8891a5);
  }

  .score-display {
    background: var(--mqa-bg-elevated, #282d38);
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 20px;
    font-family: var(--mqa-font-mono, 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .score-label {
    color: var(--mqa-text-muted, #8891a5);
  }

  .score-value {
    color: var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Question Cards */
  .question-card {
    animation: slideIn 0.4s ease;
  }

  @keyframes slideIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(20px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0); }
  }

  .q-type {
    font-family: var(--mqa-font-mono, 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .question-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--mqa-font-display, 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--mqa-text, #f0f2f5);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .question-card h3 em {
    color: var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .blank {
    display: inline-block;
    min-width: 100px;
    border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
    color: var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
  }

  .options {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .option-btn {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--mqa-bg-muted, #21252e);
    border: 2px solid var(--mqa-border, #323846);
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: var(--mqa-text-secondary, #b4bcd0);
    font-family: var(--mqa-font-sans, 'Instrument Sans', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .tf-options {
    display: grid !important;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .tf-options .option-btn {
    justify-content: center;
    height: 60px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .option-btn:hover:not(:disabled) {
    border-color: var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
    background: var(--mqa-bg-elevated, #282d38);
    color: var(--mqa-text, #f0f2f5);
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  .option-btn:disabled {
    cursor: default;
  }

  .option-btn.correct {
    border-color: #4ade80;
    background: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.15);
    color: #4ade80;
  }

  .option-btn.incorrect {
    border-color: #f87171;
    background: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.15);
    color: #f87171;
  }

  .option-btn.correct::before {
    content: "✓";
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .option-btn.incorrect::before {
    content: "✗";
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .explanation {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--mqa-bg-elevated, #282d38);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    color: var(--mqa-text-secondary, #b4bcd0);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    animation: fadeIn 0.3s ease;
  }

  .explanation strong {
    color: var(--mqa-text, #f0f2f5);
  }

  @keyframes fadeIn {
    from { opacity: 0; }
    to { opacity: 1; }
  }

  .question-footer {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }

  .next-btn {
    padding: 0.875rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--mqa-accent, #f59e0b);
